     The Tester measured on the deployed device page: four data columns render
     ("Lent to customer | Loan start date | Loan due date | Return date") plus an
     "Action" column, and the layout's FIFTH <fields> (Loan_Duration_Days__c, declared
     last) is missing. Two other related lists in this very org agree with a four-column
     render cap: the house OpenOpportunityHistory list on the Account layout declares 3
     fields and SCRUM-417 verified 3 rendered columns; my Account block declares 4 and
     renders a heading (different problem).

     Falsifiable experiment: move Loan_Duration_Days__c from last to second.
       - if the duration column now renders and the LAST field (Loan_Return_Datum__c)
         drops instead, the cause is a four-column cap, not the formula type - the fix is
         column COUNT, and AC7's five columns do not fit on a related list;
       - if the duration column is still missing and all four others render, the cause is
         the formula field type, and the derived value has to become a written field
         (which this org currently blocks: "Cannot update a field from a Formula to
         something else", and the field cannot be deleted while a class references it).

     Member name is the file base name with a DASH (skill salesforce-platform-quirks). -->
